.Dd August 14, 2026
.Dt FILEES-OPERATION 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm filees-operation
.Nd recover FileES onboarding claims and expire unfinished operations
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Cm recover
.Nm
.Op Fl config Ar path
.Cm inspect Fl -operation-id Ar uuid
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
finishes crash-visible onboarding state.
It must run as
.Sy _filees-state .
.Pp
.Cm recover
scans
.Pa operations/
for
.Pa .claim-*.json
files.
A claim-as-ticket is turned into a bundle and renamed.
A claim-as-bundle is only renamed.
It also expires unfinished operations whose TTL has elapsed, redacts OTP
and delivery address, removes expired staged keys, and resumes confirmed
realm-removal journals after every client credential has been revoked.
Active clients are not expired by the onboarding TTL.
The command is idempotent.
.Pp
.Cm inspect
prints one operation bundle.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Xr sysexits 3
values as in
.Xr filees-admin 8 .
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ doas -u _filees-state filees-operation recover
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr filees-admin 8 ,
.Xr filees-onboard 8
